/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  benzene-isopropanol -- AN NRTL PAIR FROM EVERY LABORATORY'S BUBBLE PRESSURES.

  WRITTEN BY bin/curate/pairs_px.py (DEV.md 4c C291, the P-x mirror of the
  C284 bubble-temperature pipeline; record
  docs/design/binary-pairs-from-open-measurements.md section 12).

  THE DECLARATION -- WRITTEN AND COMMITTED BEFORE ANY FIT RAN (several
  declarations of a batch share one commit).

  IDENTITY.  benzene (CAS 71-43-2, InChIKey UHOVQNZJYSORNB-UHFFFAOYSA-N)
  + isopropanol (CAS 67-63-0, InChIKey KFZMGEQAYNKOFK-UHFFFAOYSA-N), joined
  to the archive through identity.json -- never by name.  CLASS (C284): both
  records are volatile molecular liquids (no role nonvolatile/solute, no
  dissociatesTo, no charge, no solid, a vapour-pressure model), and every
  measured temperature lies below both critical temperatures.

  NO MEASURED SERIES IN THIS TREE.  constant/archiveDatasets names each
  dataset (DOI, NIST URL, article sha256, extraction selector, extract
  sha256); `bin/choupo-curate fetch` writes the points into
  constant/archiveExtracts/, which is gitignored.

  STUDIES: every isothermal bubble-pressure block of the pair at or below
  110 kPa that states an uncertainty on every point.  FITTED, ALL OF THEM
  (1 block(s), 1 laboratory(ies), 1 temperature(s)):
      10.1021/je900977e              block 5    24 pts  313.15 K  18.356-29.529 kPa  U 0.075-0.111 kPa
  SET ASIDE BY THE EXTRACTION RULES, BY NAME:
      - doi 10.1021/je900977e block 6: only 2 interior point(s) (< 5)

  THE RULE (DEV.md 4c C291, bubble-pressure pairs).  Every block above is
  fitted together; none is held out.  NRTL, a_ij = a_ji = 0, alpha = 0.30
  fixed: two parameters (b_ij, b_ji), so tau = b/T carries the temperature
  dependence.  The residual is the bubble PRESSURE at each point's stated
  temperature, RELATIVE, (P_model - P)/P; objective twoStage (least squares,
  then minimax; P_bubble relative).  OUTLIERS: after a least-squares stage over
  every point, a point with |P_model - P|/P > 20 % is discarded BY NAME
  (`discard` on its evidence entry, listed below) and the fit repeated
  without it; a STUDY with more than half of its points beyond 20 % is
  discarded whole, by name (it contradicts the model and the other
  laboratories as a whole, e.g. a composition labelled as the other member's).
  THE GRADED ACCEPTANCE (DEV.md 4c C285, in per cent of P): max |P_model - P|/P over the KEPT points is GRADED -- clean up to 5 %, warning up to 10 %, severe up to 20 %, refused above; a point with no bubble pressure refuses.  Every grade but refused is accepted and promoted (autoPromoted, humanReviewed false) with `fitGrade` and its max relative error in the record's provenance; the engine voices a warning or a severe grade on every run that reads the pair.  A pair that splits ONE liquid inside its validity span is not promoted, whatever its grade (arm f).
  Two starts: (0, 0) and (800, -400).  The per-point uncertainty U (kPa) is
  kept in each dataset and is information: this residual is already relative.

  OUTLIERS DISCARDED AFTER THE LEAST-SQUARES STAGE:
  @@OUTLIERS-BEGIN@@
      none: every one of the 24 points lies within 20 % after the
      least-squares stage.
  @@OUTLIERS-END@@

  @@MODELS-BEGIN@@
  THE OTHER ACTIVITY MODELS (DEV.md 4c C294), declared before their fits
  ran. The SAME datasets and the SAME kept points as fit_nrtl: each op
  below is fit_nrtl copied verbatim -- evidence, discards, objective,
  residual, weighting, options -- with only its parameters, its `thermo
  {}` fragment (the model) and its outputs changed; the outlier discard
  was decided ONCE, on the NRTL least-squares stage, and is reused, never
  re-decided per model. UNIQUAC: two parameters a_ij, a_ji (K), tau_ij =
  exp(-a_ij/T), b = c = 0 fixed (the NRTL default's count; temperature
  dependence 1/T), r and q each component's own record. Wilson: two
  parameters A_ij, A_ji (J/mol), Lambda_ij = (V_j/V_i) exp(-A_ij/RT), V
  the records' Vliq. Two starts each. Each model gets its own record
  (constant/parameters/<MODEL>/), its own grade at 5 / 10 / 20 % (max
  |P_model - P|/P), its own one-liquid test (arm f), `fitGradeBasis
  inSample`, the C300 cap and `review { by none; }`; a severe or refused
  grade, or a split, is not promoted. The three in-sample residuals are
  published side by side, never used to choose a model for the student.
  UNIQUAC: FITTED. Wilson: FITTED.
  @@MODELS-END@@

  @@MODELS-RESULT-BEGIN@@
  WHAT THE UNIQUAC AND WILSON FITS FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured,
  not argued). Beside fit_nrtl's max |dP|/P 1.327 % (clean) on the same
  kept points. fit_uniquac: a_ij = 154.5, a_ji = 3.5 K over 24 kept
  points: max |dP|/P 1.375 %, mean 0.832 %, graded clean -> accepted;
  fit_uniquac_start2 lands on the same pair (154.5, 3.5). PROMOTABLE by
  `bin/choupo-curate pairs --models --promote`: fit grade clean -- max
  |dP|/P 1.375 % over the 24 kept points, one liquid across the validity
  span. fit_wilson: A_ij = 1154.9, A_ji = 4979.1 J/mol over 24 kept
  points: max |dP|/P 0.305 %, mean 0.190 %, graded clean -> accepted;
  fit_wilson_start2 lands on the same pair (1154.9, 4979.1). PROMOTABLE
  by `bin/choupo-curate pairs --models --promote`: fit grade clean -- max
  |dP|/P 0.305 % over the 24 kept points, one liquid across the validity
  span.
  @@MODELS-RESULT-END@@

  @@RESULT-BEGIN@@
  WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  fit_nrtl: b_ij = 536.4 K, b_ji = 103.8 K over 24 kept points of 1
  block(s), 1 laboratory(ies), 1 temperature(s) (0 discarded): max |dP|/P
  1.33 %, mean 0.81 %, graded clean -> accepted. fit_nrtl_start2 lands on
  the same pair (536.4, 103.8). PROMOTED on 2026-11-10 into
  data/standards/parameters/NRTL/benzene-isopropanol.dat as reviewStatus
  autoPromoted, humanReviewed false, because: fit grade clean -- max
  |dP|/P 1.33 % over the 24 kept points (limits 5 / 10 / 20 %), one
  liquid across the validity span SINGLE TEMPERATURE: b/T was fitted at
  one temperature; its extrapolation is untested. SINGLE LABORATORY: one
  article's data, nothing to cross-check it.
  @@RESULT-END@@

  WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED.  The pair is correct at these temperatures in this
  frame (ideal-gas vapour, the catalogue's own vapour-pressure records); the
  measurements were transcribed by the archive and have NOT been read back
  against the articles (the CHECKLIST that `fetch` writes is the aid).
